## Who can get it

You may be able to get Access to Work if you:

- have a **disability, health condition or mental health condition** that makes some parts of work harder
- are **16 or over**
- are in **paid work**, about to start, or have a **job interview** or work trial
- live in **England, Scotland or Wales**

You do not need a diagnosis for the Mental Health Support Service.

## What it can pay for

- **special equipment** or software, such as a specialist chair or screen reader
- **adaptations** to your workplace
- **taxis or travel** to and from work if you cannot use public transport
- a **support worker**, job coach or **British Sign Language interpreter**
- **communication support** at job interviews
- the **Mental Health Support Service**, which gives free, confidential support for 9 months

## How to apply

1. Apply **online on GOV.UK** or by phone. You will need details of your job and your employer.
2. An assessor may contact you to talk about what you need.
3. You get a **grant offer** saying what will be paid for and for how long.

## Tips

- **Apply early**, ideally before you start a new job, as there can be waiting times.
- Explain the **barriers you face at work** and what would help, with examples.
- **Keep records** and submit claims promptly.
- Grants are usually reviewed after a set time, often 3 years. Reapply in good time.
